  "title": "Manila galleon trade",
  "summary": "Spanish galleons made trans-Pacific voyages between Manila and Acapulco from 1565 to 1815, carrying spices, porcelain and other luxury goods from Asia and gold and silver from the Americas. The friar and pilot Andres de Urdaneta found the eastward return, reaching Mexico on 5 October 1565, and perhaps a third of silver from New Spain and Peru went to Asia.",
